1
00:00:02,950 --> 00:00:07,215
Florida's most famous drive goes right out over the ocean!

2
00:00:07,215 --> 00:00:09,788
The first undersea park in America.

3
00:00:09,788 --> 00:00:13,097
Nearly seven miles of bridge over open water.

4
00:00:13,097 --> 00:00:15,670
And sunset at the very end of US 1!

5
00:00:16,620 --> 00:00:22,729
This is the Overseas Highway: about 100 miles from Key Largo to Key West, island to island.

6
00:00:22,729 --> 00:00:26,220
Stick around till the end for the full trip planner!

7
00:00:27,170 --> 00:00:28,336
Here's the plan!

8
00:00:28,336 --> 00:00:35,040
We start in Key Largo, then Islamorada, Marathon and Bahia Honda, and we finish in Key West!

9
00:00:35,990 --> 00:00:40,693
We're starting in Key Largo, the first big island in the Florida Keys!

10
00:00:40,693 --> 00:00:46,740
Just offshore is John Pennekamp Coral Reef State Park, the first undersea park in America.

11
00:00:46,740 --> 00:00:50,570
Hop on a glass-bottom boat, or go snorkeling on the reef!

12
00:00:51,520 --> 00:00:57,040
South on US 1, hopping from island to island, with water on both sides!

13
00:00:57,990 --> 00:01:01,979
Welcome to Islamorada, the Sportfishing Capital of the World!

14
00:01:01,979 --> 00:01:06,818
Stop at Robbie's Marina and hand-feed the giant tarpon right off the dock.

15
00:01:06,818 --> 00:01:08,060
Watch your fingers!

16
00:01:09,010 --> 00:01:14,040
Over Long Key, past the old railroad viaduct, and on to Marathon!

17
00:01:14,990 --> 00:01:18,163
Welcome to Marathon, right in the middle of the Keys!

18
00:01:18,163 --> 00:01:24,030
Take a tour of the Turtle Hospital, where injured sea turtles get patched up and sent back to sea.

19
00:01:24,980 --> 00:01:28,078
And here it is, the Seven Mile Bridge!

20
00:01:28,078 --> 00:01:33,050
Nothing but open water on both sides, for almost seven miles!

21
00:01:34,000 --> 00:01:36,216
Welcome to Bahia Honda State Park!

22
00:01:36,216 --> 00:01:42,146
Some of the best beaches in the Keys, with the old railroad bridge standing right offshore.

23
00:01:42,146 --> 00:01:43,580
Climb up for the view!

24
00:01:44,530 --> 00:01:51,010
Past Big Pine Key, where you might spot a tiny Key deer, and all the way to the end of US 1!

25
00:01:51,960 --> 00:01:54,734
We made it to Key West, Mile Marker 0!

26
00:01:54,734 --> 00:02:03,640
Snap a photo at the Southernmost Point buoy, just 90 miles from Cuba, then catch the sunset celebration at Mallory Square!

27
00:02:04,590 --> 00:02:06,196
And that's the drive!

28
00:02:06,196 --> 00:02:12,240
About 100 miles of islands and bridges, from Key Largo all the way to Key West.

29
00:02:13,190 --> 00:02:16,350
Here's your trip planner, everything in one place.

30
00:02:16,350 --> 00:02:18,120
Pause and grab a screenshot!

31
00:02:21,690 --> 00:02:23,270
Thanks for riding along!

32
00:02:23,270 --> 00:02:31,370
Subscribe to Road Trip Atlas for more Florida road trips, and next time we're crossing the Everglades on the Tamiami Trail!
